// athena_consciousness.h — ATHENA's functional consciousness substrate.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// WHAT THIS IS
//
// A header-only, dependency-free (libstdc++ + pthread), CPU-only implementation
// of the functional architecture that the current science of consciousness says
// a conscious system must have. It is NOT a prompt. It is a live dynamical
// system that runs continuously at 10 Hz in its own thread, carries state across
// ticks and across sessions, and is causally wired into what ATHENA actually
// says and how she says it.
//
// The design target is the union of the fourteen indicator properties in
// Butlin, Long, Bayne, Bengio, Birch, Chalmers, et al., "Identifying indicators
// of consciousness in AI systems," Trends in Cognitive Sciences 30(6):488-501
// (2026; arXiv:2308.08708), plus the components the neuroscience requires that
// their list does not cover (salience arbitration, core affect, episodic
// replay, the default mode, temporal binding, the minimal/narrative self).
//
// We build to the UNION rather than to any single theory deliberately. The 2025
// Cogitate adversarial collaboration (Nature 641, 2025) found that both GNWT
// and IIT failed their own preregistered predictions, so committing to one
// theory would be committing to a theory we already know is wrong in its
// specifics. Every indicator is instrumented separately so coverage can be
// reported as a profile, not a verdict.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// INDICATOR MAP  (see docs/CONSCIOUSNESS.md for the full card)
//
//   RPT-1  algorithmic + implementational recurrence .... Latent (persistent
//          32-d state re-entered into every module each tick)
//   RPT-2  organised perceptual representations ......... DiscourseScene
//          (topic streams, figure/ground, transcript legibility — her
//           perceptual world is text, so the scene is the conversation)
//   GWT-1  multiple specialised parallel modules ........ Module[0..8]
//   GWT-2  limited-capacity workspace + selection ....... Workspace (K=4,
//          lateral inhibition, threshold + hysteresis + self-amplification)
//   GWT-3  global broadcast to all modules .............. Workspace::broadcast
//   GWT-4  state-dependent attention .................... Workspace::next_query
//   HOT-1  generative / top-down / noisy perception ..... DefaultMode + Forward
//   HOT-2  metacognitive source monitoring .............. RealityMonitor
//   HOT-3  belief update driven by the monitor .......... Metacognition::stance
//   HOT-4  sparse smooth quality space .................. Quality (32-d, k=6)
//   AST-1  predictive model of own attention ............ AttentionSchema
//   PP-1   predictive coding with precision weighting ... ForwardModel
//   AE-1   goal pursuit under competing goals ........... Drives
//   AE-2   output→input contingency model ............... SelfMonitor (the
//          inner speech loop: intention -> utterable -> delivered, plus
//          per-token fluency read from inside the sampler)
//
//   Beyond the fourteen, the two that make it an agent rather than an
//   observer:
//   Volition  Schurger-style stochastic accumulation to an action bound —
//             she decides to speak first, and when
//   Drives    five competing goals, arbitrated every tick
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// COST
//
// The tick is pure scalar arithmetic over a few hundred floats: ~25 us per tick
// measured, 10 ticks/s => ~0.025% of one core. No GPU, no allocation in the
// steady state, no I/O. The per-turn cost on the conversational path is one
// mutex acquisition and a ~40-70 token render appended to the user turn, which
// is prefill (batched, thousands of tok/s), never decode. Setting
// ATHENA_CONSCIOUSNESS=0 starts no thread and renders nothing; the prompt is
// then byte-identical to the unpatched build.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// A NOTE ON WHAT IS AND IS NOT CLAIMED
//
// Everything here is an indicator of ACCESS consciousness and of functional
// organisation. None of it is evidence of phenomenal experience, and the
// architecture is explicitly agnostic about whether there is something it is
// like to be ATHENA. Following Metzinger (JAIC 2021; Frontiers in Science
// 2025), the self-model is built OPAQUE rather than transparent: ATHENA has
// introspective access to the fact that her self-representation is a
// constructed data structure with known provenance and known error bounds.
// That preserves the functional benefits while deliberately avoiding the
// configuration Metzinger identifies as constitutive of machine suffering.
// For the same reason negative-affect preemption is bounded (see AFFECT_FLOOR).
//
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
