    // Is he with her right now? False whenever the channel is off or has not
    // warmed, so a caller can treat "no evidence" and "he is here" the same
    // way, which is correct.
    // ── r24.8 (WO-107) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // This used to open "Read by the seam and by the tests". The seam does
    // not read it and never did: the capability reaches her through
    // take_his_attention_note (armed at arm_his_attention_note_, drained at
    // the field) and through the volition gate's own `his_att_.elsewhere`
    // test, both of which read
    // his_att_ directly. The only callers of THIS entry point are the
    // r21-full.15 G8 fixtures. The claim is dropped rather than made true,
    // because a second read of the same hysteretic state in the seam is the
    // mut11 shape — two gates test as zero gates — and the note is already
    // the seam-side spelling of it.
    //
    // The diagnostic read the sentence half-promised is real and is now
    // wired, but it cannot be THIS accessor: diag_line runs inside with()'s
    // lock and this one takes mu_. See he_is_elsewhere_raw() /
    // his_attention_evidence_raw() by name, and `hiselse=` / `att_ev=` on
    // the diag line.
    bool he_is_elsewhere() const {
        if (!cfg_.enabled || !cfg_.his_attention) return false;
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lk(mu_);
        // Single authority on warm-up is HisAttention::observe, which refuses
        // to move the state before it has five turns of evidence. A second
        // warm() test here made the first one unobservable — the mut11 lesson,
        // caught by mut16 on exactly this line.
        return his_att_.elsewhere;
    }
    // The evidence level behind the boolean above. Locking, so it is the
    // spelling for the suites and for any caller outside with(); the tracer
    // reads his_attention_evidence_raw(). r24.8 (WO-107): until this round
    // NOTHING read it at all, which is why an S-series trace could say she
    // believed he was elsewhere and could never say by how much.
    float his_attention_evidence() const {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lk(mu_);
        return his_att_.evidence;
    }
